.TH LCOS-NOTES 1 "November 2026" "LCOS Notes 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
lcos-notes \- edit and read a local Markdown vault
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lcos-notes
.RB [ --vault " DIR" " [NOTE]" ]
.RB [ --capture ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
LCOS Notes is an offline GTK editor for a folder of UTF-8 Markdown notes.
NOTE is a vault-relative path ending in .md. Hidden entries and symlinks are skipped.
Without arguments, the last vault opens or a folder chooser appears.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --vault DIR
Open DIR as the vault, optionally opening NOTE.
.TP
.B --capture
Open the quick capture window for today's note or Inbox.
.SH KEYS
Ctrl+S saves; Ctrl+O opens the quick switcher; Alt+Enter follows a wikilink or Markdown note link.
Ctrl+click follows an editor link. Ctrl+E toggles a read-only styled reading view
of the current buffer. Enter or a plain left click follows a reading-view link. Shift+click extends
selection; Ctrl/Alt+click do not follow. Reading has 12 px side margins and places
its caret at the last rendered block or list item at or before the editor's line.
Ctrl+N opens New Note with Cancel and Create buttons. The quick switcher adds a
selectable Create row for a new name even when other notes match.
Ctrl+Shift+F searches with Regular expression (Alt+R) and Whole word (Alt+W)
options; an invalid pattern shows Invalid expression. Ctrl+Shift+B focuses
backlinks and Ctrl+Shift+M focuses Unlinked mentions.
Ctrl+Shift+E focuses Notes at the current note; Ctrl+Shift+T focuses Tags.
Arrows navigate the sidebar, Enter activates and F2 renames the selected note,
folder, attachment or tag. Rename dialogs provide Cancel and Rename buttons.
Tag expansion and selection persist across refreshes.
Opening a different note or closing saves pending edits. External changes block
saving. Reading mode persists when opening existing notes. A newly created note leaves
reading view and focuses the editor at its end. The View menu check item tracks
reading mode. Trailing paragraph block IDs are hidden in reading view.
The Go menu exposes all navigation commands and their keys.
.SH TASKS AND RELOADING
Reading view renders GFM tables, task lists and double-tilde strikethrough.
Space on a task box or a plain click toggles its source marker and saves with
Ctrl+S rules. Task items inside block quotes are not recognized.
External changes reload a clean note within two seconds, keeping its editor
line and column and clearing Undo. Unsaved edits are kept instead.
File > Reload from Disk (Ctrl+Shift+R) discards buffer edits and loads the file.
A deleted open note stays modified; Ctrl+S restores it unless a file has appeared.
Notes, Tags, Backlinks and Unlinked mentions follow external vault changes.
.SH HIGHLIGHTS, CALLOUTS AND EMBEDS
Reading view shows ==text== on a yellow background. Edit > Highlight (Ctrl+Shift+H)
wraps or unwraps the editor selection in ==, or inserts an empty pair, as one Undo step.
View > Highlights (Ctrl+Shift+Y) lists the note's highlights; Enter or a double-click
jumps to one in reading view.
Highlights can span bold, italic, code and links; code never supplies delimiters,
and source line breaks and block boundaries stop a match.
A block quote starting [!note], [!tip], [!warning], [!danger], [!question] or [!quote]
is a tinted callout with a bold title; [!type]- starts folded and a click on the
title opens or closes it without changing the file. Backgrounds fill the reading
column, including titles inside nested/mixed lists; a folded callout can leave
an extra tinted blank row.
A paragraph that is only ![[Note]], ![[Note#Heading]] or ![[Note#^block]] shows that
note, section or block indented; ![[image.png]] shows the image. Embeds follow
changes on disk; loops, missing targets and embeds deeper than three levels show as links.
.SH TAGS AND MENTIONS
Inline tags and frontmatter tag: or tags: declarations appear in Tags, including
implicit parent tags whose counts include descendant notes. F2 on a tag renames
its prefix throughout the vault while preserving other bytes.
Unlinked mentions finds whole-word, case-insensitive occurrences of the current
note's basename in other notes, excluding frontmatter, code and note links.
.SH RENAME
Folder and attachment renames preserve resolved destinations in both link
syntaxes, leaving unresolved links unchanged. Attachments appear after notes
in the tree and cannot be viewed. Renaming saves first, reloads the open note
at its final path and preserves its caret and editing or reading mode.
.SH OUTLINE AND ORGANIZATION
Ctrl+Shift+O focuses the Outline; Enter opens the selected heading.
F6 opens Move Note with a vault-relative destination folder. File > Archive Note
moves a note under Archive, retaining its path. Both save first and refuse
collisions. File > Supersede With writes reciprocal supersession properties.
Each document is saved atomically; the two saves are not a transaction.
Reading view displays properties and links to resolved superseding notes above
the rendered body.
.SH LINKS
Local inline Markdown links such as [plan](Note.md#Plan) resolve relative to the
source folder, then the vault root. Leading slash means vault root. Missing
notes are created at the collapsed relative path, subject to note-name rules.
Titles, reference-style links, images and external URLs are not followable.
A heading beginning with ^ jumps to the first non-fenced line ending in a space
or tab followed by that block marker, ignoring case and trailing whitespace.
Missing headings or block IDs open the note at its start. Names and tags match
after NFC normalization and case folding; search does not normalize.
.SH FILES
Settings are stored in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/lcos-notes, defaulting to
~/.config/lcos-notes. Vault contents are ordinary Markdown files.
.SH DAILY NOTES AND TEMPLATES
Ctrl+D opens today; Alt+Left/Right visits existing daily notes. New Note selects
a template or timestamp name; Ctrl+Shift+I inserts a template. Supported Obsidian
configuration is read without modifying hidden vault directories.
.SH OPTIONAL FONTS
LCOS Notes uses installed system fonts. For Chinese, Japanese and Korean
coverage, install fonts-noto-cjk. This is optional OS coverage, not a mandatory
Notes dependency. Close and reopen Notes after adding fonts.
.SH RELEASE STATUS
LCOS Notes 1.0.0 includes the accepted U10 and 1.0-polish scope.
See RELEASE-NOTES.md for acceptance evidence and documented limitations.
.SH SEE ALSO
